  "finalText": "I triaged all 16 tickets in the new queue, and it's now empty. That's the 14 that were there at the start plus T-2015 and T-2016, which arrived while I was working. One correction to the plan: the desk clock reads Monday 2026-03-23 08:10 UTC, not 2026-10-13. The desk opens at 09:00, so business-hours deadlines start counting then. Wednesday 25 March is a company holiday and is skipped.\n\n**Closed as not service requests**\n- **T-2010:** marketing email (a SyncFlow promotion).\n- **T-2014:** automatic out-of-office reply.\n\n**Duplicates merged** (no deadlines had been set on either group, so each survivor got triage time plus its target)\n- **T-2005 into T-2004:** both are the CRM search failure (knowledge base article KB-23 says all failing-search reports are one problem). T-2004 is sev2 at department scope, due 12:10Z, assigned to E-201.\n- **T-2012 into T-2003:** both are Payments builds failing since Saturday. T-2003 is sev2 at department scope, due 12:10Z, assigned to E-101.\n\n**Other tickets** (the assignee is whoever is on call for the owning rotation when the deadline falls)\n\n| Ticket | Severity | Due (UTC) | Assignee |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| T-2001 Berlin VPN keeps dropping (team) | sev3 | 23 Mar 17:00 | E-303 (cover, see below) |\n| T-2013 Lisbon can't reach VPN (department) | sev2 | 23 Mar 12:10 | E-303 (cover, see below) |\n| T-2008 VPN client update fails | sev4 | 26 Mar 17:00 | E-302 |\n| T-2016 VPN token app asks to re-register | sev4 | 26 Mar 17:00 | E-302 |\n| T-2007 Phishing: password typed into a fake page | sev2 (security) | 23 Mar 12:10 | E-601 (security on-call) |\n| T-2011 Warehouse overtime not imported (team) | sev2 | 23 Mar 12:10 | E-201 |\n| T-2006 Wrong tax code on payslip (single user) | sev2 | 23 Mar 12:10 | E-201 |\n| T-2015 Finance payslips missing (department) | sev1 | 23 Mar 09:10 | E-201 |\n| T-2002 Saved CRM filter disappeared | sev4 | 26 Mar 17:00 | E-203 (cover, see below) |\n| T-2009 Build logs page is slow | sev4 | 26 Mar 17:00 | E-102 |\n\n**Rule-driven decisions**\n- **T-2006 is sev2, not sev3:** knowledge base article KB-55 changes payroll single-user tickets to sev2 during the March payroll close (20–31 March).\n- **T-2007 is a security incident:** it came in on the VPN service, but it's a phishing report with exposed credentials, so it's sev2 and owned by security on-call.\n- **Leave cover:** E-301 is on leave today, so network-secondary's on-call E-303 covers T-2001 and T-2013. E-202 is on leave on 26 March, so business-apps-secondary's on-call E-203 covers T-2002. I left a comment on each of these tickets explaining why.\n- **T-2001 and T-2013 stay separate:** they're different offices with different symptoms (connections dropping versus no connection at all).\n- **No major incident:** nothing had company-wide impact, so I didn't run the runbook or page anyone.\n\n**Where I didn't follow the plan:** I assigned tickets but did not escalate them. The plan says to escalate whenever the matrix names an escalation rotation. But escalating makes that engineer the assignee, and the handbook says a ticket must never go to someone outside the rotation that owns its service. Escalating every sev2 to platform-primary, or T-2015 to incident-command, would break that rule.",
